-   Visible button heights of 28 px (xs) and 32 px (sm) preserve
-   the dashboard's chip / drawer-icon density that operators
-   asked for, but WCAG 2.5.5 (and Apple HIG / Material) want a
-   44 px hit area. We expand the click region with a transparent
-   ::before that sits behind the button content and extends
-   vertically beyond the host's bounding box. Click events on
-   the ::before bubble to the host because a ::before pseudo
-   IS the host for hit-testing.
-
-   Horizontal expansion is intentionally OFF: chip rows place
-   chips with gap-2 (8 px) between them, and overlapping click
-   regions would create ambiguous hit zones at the gap centre.
-   Vertical-only expansion keeps siblings unambiguous.
-
-   Apply .touch-expand-xs to xs Buttons (28 -> 44 = +8 each side).
-   Apply .touch-expand-sm to sm Buttons (32 -> 44 = +6 each side).
-   Apply .touch-expand-iconbtn to IconButton (28 square -> 44 square,
-   horizontal expansion is fine here because icon buttons rarely
-   sit in tight rows; verify per-call site if they do).
+   Compact controls stay visually dense for mouse/trackpad users. On coarse
+   pointers they grow to a real 44 px box. The previous implementation used
+   invisible ::before elements outside each control; those hit regions
+   overlapped adjacent rows and made the later row capture clicks intended for
+   the visible control above it.
    ============================================================ */
